 "result_text": "`Local` commands can now take `local` as an optional third argument to `prepare`, so `def prepare(self, args, parser, local)` from the issue works. The existing test suite has 3 failures, all caused by this change.\n\nThe change is in `src/argcmdr.py`. `Command.call` now builds its argument list from a new `get_extra_call_args` hook, which returns nothing by default. `Local` overrides the hook to pass `self.local` when the target is `prepare`. As with `args` and `parser`, the argument is only passed if `prepare` declares a parameter for it.\n\nThe 3 failures are `TestPrepareCallSignature::test_bad`, `test_fancy` and `test_tricky`, which all passed before my change. They use a third parameter named `lang` (`prepare(self, args, parser, lang)` or `lang='en'`) and expect it to stay at its default or to be rejected. Under the new behavior that third positional slot receives `local` instead. I left the tests alone, as you asked, so they will need updating to match.",
